      ":question/id": "9e5ada32-5b77-5b60-9c13-e846f4bf8123",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n2\\,\\sin\\left(75^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(75^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(150^\\circ\\right).\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=75^\\circ$ and then at $x=150^\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\sin\\left(150^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(150^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\sin\\left(300^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(300^\\circ\\right)=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
